description:
Design a simple clock-driven toggle circuit that alternates the state of an output LED at a frequency of 1 Hz. The module increments a counter on each rising edge of a 50 MHz clock signal, and when the counter reaches 50 million, it flips the state of the output `estado`, which is mapped to the first LED output. The second LED output is unused in this design.
module top_module(
	input CLOCK_50,
	output [1:0] LEDG
	);

code:
module top_module(
	input CLOCK_50,
	output [1:0] LEDG
	);reg estado =0;
	reg [32:0]cont = 0;

   	assign LEDG[0] = estado;

	always @(posedge CLOCK_50) begin
		if (cont == 50000000) begin		
	      		estado = ~estado;
       	    		cont = 0;
	   	end 
	   	else begin
        		cont <= cont + 1;
	   	end
	end
endmodule

