description:
Design a frequency divider that generates an output clock signal (clk_out) by dividing the input clock signal (clk_in) by a factor of 2 raised to the power of n. The module includes a counter that increments on each edge of the input clock signal, toggling the output clock when the counter reaches a specified maximum value, thereby achieving the desired clock division ratio.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter n = 1; // number of times to divide the input clock signal by 2

reg [n-1:0] counter;
wire clk_edge;

assign clk_edge = clk_in ^ ~clk_in;

always @(posedge clk_edge) begin
  if (counter == (2**n)-1) begin
    clk_out <= ~clk_out;
    counter <= 0;
  end else begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
  end
end

endmodule

