description:
Design a priority encoder that takes in a set of 8 input signals and outputs the binary representation of the index of the highest active input. The module continuously monitors the input signals and, upon detecting the highest priority input (the leftmost bit set), encodes its index into a 3-bit output. If no inputs are active, the output defaults to zero. This encoder facilitates efficient signal handling by providing a compact representation of the active input's priority.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output reg [log2_n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output reg [log2_n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 8; // number of input signals
localparam log2_n = $clog2(n); // Calculate the logarithm base 2 of n

always @* begin
  casez(in) // priority encoder logic
    8'b10000000: out = 3'b000; // highest priority input
    8'b01000000: out = 3'b001;
    8'b00100000: out = 3'b010;
    8'b00010000: out = 3'b011;
    8'b00001000: out = 3'b100;
    8'b00000100: out = 3'b101;
    8'b00000010: out = 3'b110;
    8'b00000001: out = 3'b111;
    default: out = 3'b000; // default output
  endcase
end

endmodule

