Design a touch sensor interface that detects when a touch signal is activated while implementing debouncing logic to prevent false triggers from noise. The module features a parameterized sensitivity and debounce time, utilizing a simple low-pass filter to clean the incoming signal. It employs a debounce counter to ensure the touch state is stable before registering a touch event, outputting a high signal only when a valid touch is detected. This interface effectively allows for reliable touch detection in responsive applications.
