description:
Design a circular shift register known as a ring counter with a specified width of n bits (default set to 8). On each rising edge of the clock signal, the counter shifts its bits to the right, moving the last bit to the first position, thus creating a repetitive pattern of bits around the register. The output captures the current state of the ring counter.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 8; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= {counter[n-2:0], counter[n-1]};
end

assign out = counter;

endmodule

