description:
Design a dual-function D flip-flop (DFF) with asynchronous reset (R) and set (S) controls. The output Q captures the value of input D at the negative edge of the clock signal C, unless reset is asserted (R=0), which sets Q to LOW, or set is asserted (S=1), which sets Q to HIGH. The module includes timing specifications for different FPGA architectures, ensuring proper setup and hold times for D and R signals with respect to the clock edge.
module top_module(
	output reg Q,
	input C, R, D, S
);

code:
module top_module(
	output reg Q,
	input C, R, D, S
);always @(negedge C) begin
		if (R == 1'b0) begin
			Q <= 1'b0;
		end else if (S == 1'b1) begin
			Q <= 1'b1;
		end else begin
			Q <= D;
		end
	end

`ifdef ICE40_HX
	specify
		$setup(D, negedge C, 21);
		$setup(R, negedge C, 9);
		$hold(Q, negedge C, 10);
	endspecify
`endif

`ifdef ICE40_LP
	specify
		$setup(D, negedge C, 33);
		$setup(R, negedge C, 15);
		$hold(Q, negedge C, 15);
	endspecify
`endif

`ifdef ICE40_U
	specify
		$setup(D, negedge C, 45);
		$setup(R, negedge C, 21);
		$hold(Q, negedge C, 20);
	endspecify
`endif

endmodule

